FREECULI ZC-CORE METHODOLOGY
DUAL-LICENSING FRAMEWORK

The FreeCuli ZC-CORE Architecture and the underlying AIoT/Edge AI methodology operate under a strict Dual-Licensing Model.

======================================================================
1. HARDWARE LICENSE (CERN-OHL-S v2.0)
======================================================================
All hardware designs, PCB schematics, and physical isolation architectures are licensed under the CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S v2.0).

Anyone combining or distributing these hardware designs MUST share their derivative hardware schematics openly under the same license, UNLESS a Commercial Exemption License is acquired.

======================================================================
2. SOFTWARE LICENSE (AGPL-3.0)
======================================================================
All associated software, controllers, and firmware logic are licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0).

======================================================================
COMMERCIAL EXEMPTION (B2B)
======================================================================
Manufacturers wishing to integrate the ZC-CORE methodology without open-sourcing their proprietary designs must obtain a Commercial Exemption License.

For full legal definitions, patent retaliation clauses, and trademark usage policies, refer strictly to the official zero-cloud-dual-licensing.md document within this repository.

